            <div xml:id="d818">

                <pb facs="1091" n="981" sameAs="frus:frus1928v03/pg981"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48 Refugees 67/5: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Angora</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-01-12T11:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 12,
                                1928—11 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:15
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>1. Department’s 4, January 7, 4 p.m. The assistance of American citizens is
                    appreciated by the Turkish Government, which will grant a delay of 12 months for
                    the evacuation of Russian refugees, with <pb facs="1092" n="982" xml:id="pg982"
                    /> the exception of 30 or 40 who have conducted political propaganda. The
                    Turkish Minister for Foreign Affairs asks that this concession not be revealed
                    prior to its official announcement here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
